{
  "_comment": [
    "Default bindings for the eight slots this package declares - two physical ports and the",
    "six a multitap adds. The frontend ships no bindings of its own: a package that declares a",
    "controller says how it is played by default, and the user's own bindings always win.",
    "",
    "The face buttons follow the pad's own geometry rather than a keyboard's alphabet:",
    "Cross is the bottom one and takes the key under the hand, Circle the right, Square",
    "the left, Triangle the top. The shoulders sit above and below each other the way they",
    "do on the controller. Analog is a real button on a DualShock 2 - it switches the pad",
    "between digital and analog mode, which a game can see - so it is bound rather than",
    "assumed.",
    "",
    "Player 1 keeps the keyboard as well as the first pad; players 2 to 8 get a pad each and",
    "no keys, because eight people at one keyboard is not a thing and any key chosen for them",
    "would collide with player 1's. The instruments' controls - the frets, the strum bar, the",
    "Negcon's buttons, Pop'n Music's nine - are declared but unbound: they belong to devices a",
    "port has to be SET to, and a binding for a device nobody plugged in is a key that does",
    "nothing."
  ],
